@kitlangton 
Running into the same issue with deepseek-v4-flash-free when `format` option is given while calling from opencode sdk.

```js
{
  message: "Error from provider (DeepSeek): Thinking mode does not support this tool_choice",
  statusCode: 400,
  isRetryable: false,
  responseHeaders: {
    "cf-placement": "remote-ORD",
    "cf-ray": "a0237c8998767f72-IAD",
    connection: "keep-alive",
    "content-length": "178",
    "content-type": "application/octet-stream",
    date: "Wed, 27 May 2026 08:00:33 GMT",
    server: "cloudflare",
  },
  responseBody: "{\"error\":{\"message\":\"Error from provider (DeepSeek): Thinking mode does not support this tool_choice\",\"type\":\"invalid_request_error\",\"param\":null,\"code\":\"invalid_request_error\"}}",
  metadata: {
    url: "https://opencode.ai/zen/v1/chat/completions",
  },
}
```

I am calling it like this

```typescript
import { createOpencodeClient } from "@opencode-ai/sdk"
import { z } from "zod"

const oc = createOpencodeClient({
  baseUrl: `http://localhost:${process.env.OPENCODE_SERVER_PORT}`,
  responseStyle: "data",
})

const main = async () => {
  const response = await oc.session.prompt({
    query: { directory: folderLocation },
    path: { id: sessionId },
    body: {
      model: { providerID: "opencode", modelID: "deepseek-v4-flash-free" },
      agent: "build",
      tools: { question: false },
      parts: [{ type: "text", text: ["my prompt here"] }],
      // @ts-expect-error - format is not supported in the opencode SDK types, but it is supported in the API
      format: { type: "json_schema", schema: z.toJSONSchema(MySchema) }
    },
  })
}

main()
```

This even messes up the OpenCode Desktop app when that particular session is clicked. You'll have to delete the session or affected messages from sqlite for the app to function again.

FYI, following settings seems to work for 1.15.10. 
no freezes so far  

"provider": {
    "openai": {
      "options": {
        "timeout": 180000,
        "chunkTimeout": 30000
      }
    }
  },
